  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-02T22:25:36.465Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Allow the height of the avatar collision volume with the world to be either specified explicitly by the creator, or set according to the actual bounding height of the avatar.\n\nCurrently, avatar collision uses a fixed height regardless of the actual bounds of the avatar mesh. This results in short avatars getting their 'head' caught on low hanging geometry that otherwise appears to them as passable. This is worse for short flying avatars like fairies who want to fly at eye level with other players. Low ceilings and doorframes will limit their vertical movement and force them to remain at the feet of other players.\n\n[AvatarOverhaul]",
